// Seven equal bars on a 3:5 field.
vexyl 1
meta {
  name "Transfeminine flag"
  encoder "Naomi Persephone Amethyst"
  license "CC-BY-SA-4.0"
  render-license "CC0-1.0"
  series "transfeminine-flag"
  version "blue-and-pink"
  source "https://www.deviantart.com/pride-flags/art/Trans-Woman-Transfeminine-%281%29-543925985"
  source "https://lgbtqia.fandom.com/wiki/Transfeminine"
  note "The designer and first publication were not found. The earliest copy read is 'Trans Woman / Transfeminine (1)' by Pride-Flags on DeviantArt, published 2015-07-04 UTC (3 July, Pacific time), which credits no one and gives no meanings. The LGBTQIA+ Wiki (Fandom) says its creator and meanings are unknown. It is the counterpart of the transmasculine flag, posted by the same account the same evening; an all-pink alternative, 'Trans Woman / Transfeminine (3)' of 14 June 2016, is not written here."
  note "Construction and colors are read from that post's image (5000 by 3000 PNG), which is not shown to be the designer's: seven bars of 429, 426, 433, 424, 433, 426 and 429 pixels, taken as equal, #73deff, #ffe0ed, #ffb5d5, #ff8cbe, #ffb5d5, #ffe0ed, #73deff. The 3:5 proportion is the image's."
}
palette {
  blue "#73deff"
  pale-pink "#ffe0ed"
  light-pink "#ffb5d5"
  pink "#ff8cbe"
}
proportion hoist=3 fly=5

bars blue pale-pink light-pink pink light-pink pale-pink blue
